{"id": "EUVD-2026-76544", "enisaUuid": "d27f89db-c411-3b48-846e-3be91b75db4b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix use-before-check of ReparseDataLength in reparse_buf_ptr()\n\nreparse_buf_ptr() reads buf->ReparseDataLength before checking that\ncount covers the full fixed header:\n\n    buf = (struct reparse_data_buffer *)((u8 *)io + off);\n    len = sizeof(*buf);                          /* 8 bytes */\n    rdlen = le16_to_cpu(buf->ReparseDataLength); /* offset 4, 2 bytes */\n\n    if (count < len || count < rdlen + len)      /* check comes after */\n\nstruct reparse_data_buffer has ReparseDataLength at offset 4.  If a\nserver returns OutputCount < 6, the read at offset 4-5 reaches past\nthe end of the received data.  The off+count bounds against iov_len\nwere already validated, but that does not protect against count being\nsmaller than sizeof(*buf).\n\nSplit the check: verify count >= sizeof(*buf) before reading\nReparseDataLength, then verify count covers the data region.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:04", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b70bc592afd19732e2e4563300ebe8f974280365", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/711cf71300d7992f450600df8864917d3538679f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/05f78e6cf34ea3a285053bd5999e08e8ac298bd5"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j6wx-7c3w-595c", "CVE-2026-89632"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.55, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c37198a-42a3-3899-bfa1-7a6ed912982b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67ec9949b0dfe78c99e110dd975eb7dc5645630c <05f78e6cf34ea3a285053bd5999e08e8ac298bd5"}, {"id": "4553118e-7f6b-32b2-afad-e6c624bec00f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a158bb66b1373866d9fd5997565a58a573085539 <b70bc592afd19732e2e4563300ebe8f974280365"}, {"id": "63a9d74b-3230-33aa-82b0-2386218a28bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "8b9c52e5-566d-3861-84ed-da34a944df39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "bb91a274-c8cb-3895-909f-ba0f6cb56b36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "da279c26-f70b-3ab1-aee8-6b1b0e7dcdc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e102c8b7-3fad-30f5-b8e3-8778d2216bc6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67ec9949b0dfe78c99e110dd975eb7dc5645630c <711cf71300d7992f450600df8864917d3538679f"}, {"id": "e37ed4f5-53e6-3dfc-9de7-bb37136e0a62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "f92b58a9-6198-39cc-a216-06335b5fe58e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.32 <6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f4c844f4-c33c-38e4-8577-1a58783113ea", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}